From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: igloo <nix@local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:12:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg: emit fastsnap edge coverage into every translated
 block

One call in translator_loop(), which is the only place a block-entry hook
can live and still be correct.

cpu_tb_exec() is the obvious alternative and it is wrong: chained blocks
jump straight to each other and never return through it, so a counter
there sees the first block of a chain and nothing else. Instrumenting at
translation time puts the edge log inside the generated code, where the
chain cannot route around it.

It has to be a call rather than a conditional in the target frontends
because the fourteen targets have fourteen frontends and this is the one
generic point they all pass through. translator_loop() is compiled once
per user/system flavour, so CONFIG_USER_ONLY is available and the hook is
excluded from the linux-user build, where there is no fastsnap.

WHY NOT A TCG PLUGIN. Plugins are built here -- configure enables them
whenever a C++ compiler is present, so the shipped libqemu-system-armel.so
exports 89 qemu_plugin_* symbols despite configs/default.json never naming
--enable-plugins. They are still the wrong tool, for two reasons:

  - A plugin cannot see the reset. The map has to be summarised and
    cleared in the same bottom half that rewinds guest RAM. Penguin embeds
    QEMU as a library and drives it over the CFFI ABI; a plugin is loaded
    by QEMU and has no channel back to the embedding process.

  - The plugin API cannot express an edge. Its inline ops are exactly
    ADD_U64 and STORE_U64 against a fixed scoreboard entry, with no
    indexed addressing, so map[prev ^ cur]++ has to become a per-block
    callback -- an indirect call per translated block, against the seven
    inline TCG ops this emits.

Costs nothing when unused: fastsnap_cov_translate() returns on a single
global bool before touching the TCG context, and nothing calls it in a
build that never arms coverage.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Patch-Set: fastsnap
---
 accel/tcg/translator.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/translator.c b/accel/tcg/translator.c
index cd7d079fe050bcba229905bfd1de3df659264e81..6dad3db1c68f2dcd09623c874898b2ec7bb6509d 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/translator.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/translator.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include "exec/target_page.h"
 #include "exec/translator.h"
 #include "exec/plugin-gen.h"
+#include "fastsnap/coverage.h"
 #include "tcg/tcg-op-common.h"
 #include "internal-common.h"
 #include "disas/disas.h"
@@ -153,6 +154,20 @@ void translator_loop(CPUState *cpu, TranslationBlock *tb, int *max_insns,
     ops->tb_start(db, cpu);
     tcg_debug_assert(db->is_jmp == DISAS_NEXT);  /* no early exit */
 
+#ifndef CONFIG_USER_ONLY
+    /*
+     * fastsnap edge coverage. Emitted once per block, ahead of the first
+     * instruction, so it runs however the block is entered -- including via a
+     * chained jump from another block, which never returns to cpu_tb_exec()
+     * and is why this cannot live there instead.
+     *
+     * A no-op unless coverage is armed, and it emits nothing at all for a
+     * block outside the configured address range, so a filtered block carries
+     * no runtime cost rather than a cheap one. See include/fastsnap/coverage.h.
+     */
+    fastsnap_cov_translate(db->pc_first);
+#endif
+
     plugin_enabled = plugin_gen_tb_start(cpu, db);
     db->plugin_enabled = plugin_enabled;
 
